# SBC5 Control Center — Home Assistant Integration

**English** · [Polski](#polski)

> HACS-managed Home Assistant companion integration for SBC5 Control Center on Raspberry Pi 5.

**Version {{VERSION}} · Home Assistant ≥ {{HA_CORE_MIN}} · Apache-2.0**

## English

### Important requirement

This repository contains the **Home Assistant integration only**. It is **not a standalone replacement for the SBC5 Control Center App**.

> **The SBC5 Control Center App/runtime must be installed and running.**

Main project and required App: **[krlmdfk/sbc5-control-center](https://github.com/krlmdfk/sbc5-control-center)**

The App provides Raspberry Pi 5 host telemetry and control services. This HACS integration exposes them natively in Home Assistant through entities, device information, diagnostics and update/restart state.

### Current release

{{SUMMARY_EN}}

### Repository relationship

| Repository | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **[sbc5-control-center](https://github.com/krlmdfk/sbc5-control-center)** | Main project and required App/runtime. |
| **[sbc5-control-center-integration](https://github.com/krlmdfk/sbc5-control-center-integration)** | HACS-managed Home Assistant integration. |

### Installation

1. Install and run the SBC5 Control Center App/runtime from the main project.
2. In HACS add `https://github.com/krlmdfk/sbc5-control-center-integration` as **Custom repository → Integration**.
3. Install **SBC5 Control Center**.
4. Restart Home Assistant when requested.

